d exploration is to replace states in the policy rollout with the corresponding demonstration states when the states are too far away from the reference. For a threshold \u03f5:\nst+1 = { T (st, at), at \u223c \u03c0\u03b8(a|st) if \u2225st \u2212 s\u0302t\u222522 < \u03f5 T (s\u0302t, at), at \u223c \u03c0\u03b8(a|s\u0302t) otherwise.\n(3.5)\nSince the criterion for choosing which states to replace is based on the performance of the current rollout, the replacing frequency dynamic adjusts itself during the model training."
